  "question": {
    "text": "A resistance $\\mathrm{R}$ and inductance $\\mathrm{L}$ and a capacitor $\\mathrm{C}$ all are connected in series with an AC supply. The resistance of $\\mathrm{R}$ is 16 ohm and for a given frequency, the inductive reactance of $L$ is 24 ohm and capacitive reactance of $\\mathrm{C}$ is $12 \\mathrm{ohm} .$ If the current in the circuit is 5 amp., find the potential difference across $\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{L}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "c2cyU",
      "text": "30,20,50 volt",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
